1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Among Terminal - native workspaces and live terminals

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Ctrl+Shift+T: create and name another project workspace

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Background terminals stay alive; hide and show the sidebar

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Ctrl+Shift+N: split the current terminal

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Split again: each terminal keeps its own project directory

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Ctrl+Shift+Arrow: resize without leaving the keyboard

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Drag the divider with the mouse to resize live terminals

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Drag a pane header onto an edge to rearrange the nested layout

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Alt+Arrow: move pane focus; click a terminal to focus it directly

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Ctrl+Shift+X: zoom one pane, then restore the layout

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Live resource meters above; each pane's path below; clock at bottom right

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Ctrl+, opens Settings: shortcuts and independent plugins

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Disable Clock in Plugins: its process and footer disappear

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Enable Clock again: the live footer returns

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Ctrl+Page Up / Down: return to the still-running background project

16
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Restart Among: restore names, layouts and directories only after consent

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Choose Restore: fresh shells reopen in their separate directories

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
F11: fullscreen; press again to restore the window

19
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,050
Ctrl+Shift+W: close a pane and keep typing in its surviving sibling
